## Authentication & Authorization

- Bearer tokens live in **httpOnly cookies**, set by Next Route Handlers acting as a BFF. Browser JavaScript never holds a token.
- Two Sanctum guards, two token namespaces — `auth:user` and `auth:admin`. Separate cookie names, separate Route Handler namespaces, separate refresh endpoints. Never send an admin token to a user route or vice versa.
- **Refresh on 401, not 403.** The backend returns 401 for expired/absent credentials, 403 for policy denial. Refresh once, then fail — queue concurrent requests behind the in-flight refresh.
- Refresh sends the token in the **JSON body**, not an auth header.
- Three authorization layers, one real authority: edge middleware (UX redirect only) → Server Component render (never ship markup the user can't use) → Laravel Policies (**the only real authority**).

